# Scaffold templates are embedded into the CLI byte for byte and become the
# files a generated project contains. Git's autocrlf converts text files on
# checkout, so without this a clone on Windows gets CRLF templates, the CLI
# embeds CRLF, and every generated project differs from the one CI verified.
#
# Found the day the templates moved out of Go string literals (v3.338.0): the
# repair constants stopped matching the templates they mirror, and only on
# Windows, because CI runs on Linux where no conversion happens. The same shape
# as v3.333, where the compose repairs had never once run on a Windows checkout.
internal/scaffold/templates/** text eol=lf

# The scaffolder reads these and writes their contents into projects too.
*.tmpl text eol=lf
